-- title:
--   A maximal ideal of the j-chart lying over a supersingular place
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a nonunit of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M')$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places, i.e. those places $w$ that are rational, satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace` and have $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of `jGeomGen` lying in `ssJSet q`; assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, i.e. the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the full level-$M'$ modular function field is contained in that of the $X_H$-function field of level $q^2M'$ with $H$ the kernel of reduction of units to $\mathbb Z/q$. Let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A,M')$ (a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of the source containing the image of $A$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with residues of constants, together with a map on places preserving degrees and orders), and assume that every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ belongs to $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and has $R_0$-residue equal, as a Laurent series over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, to the coefficientwise residue of $y$. Fix $s\in W$. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ an element lying in $A$; write $A_0=A\cap k_0$ for the comap of $A$ along $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and assume $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, henselian, with algebraically closed residue field, and that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$. Let $\ell'\ne q$ be a prime, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $k_0\subseteq k_0((q))$ given by the $k_0$-base change $\mathrm{laurentBaseChange}$ of $\mathrm{xHFunctionField}\,((q\ell')^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell')\,M')$, equipped with an $A_0$-algebra structure compatible with $A_0\to k_0\to K$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with underlying Laurent series $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,k_0\,\mathrm{jq}$, and assume $\mathrm{qExpand}\,k_0\,\ell'(\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,k_0\,\mathrm{jq})$ lies in $K$ and, as an element of $K$, in $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K\,j$, the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A_0[j]$. Then there is a maximal ideal $y$ of $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K\,j$ containing the image of $\pi_0$ and such that the following holds for every Laurent series $g$ over $\mathbb Q$ in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M'$: if the image of $g$ in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, if every place $P$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of $\mathrm{jq}$ nonnegative also has $P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of $g$ nonnegative, and if the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, then for any proof that $\mathrm{qExpand}\,k_0\,\ell'(\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,k_0\,g)$ lies in $K$ and in $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K\,j$, and for every $c\in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$ and whose residue in $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference of that element of the chart algebra and the image of $c$ lies in $y$.
--
--   This produces a closed point of the special fibre of the $j$-finite chart of the level-$(q\ell')^2M'$ integral model which lies over the prescribed supersingular place $s$ of the level-$M'$ reduction, the congruences recording that the point specialises the $\ell'$-twisted expansions $g(q^{\ell'})$ to the values $g(s)$. It is the existence half used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_isMaximal_chartAlgFin_mem_ssJSet_over_of_ssPlaces`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_isMaximal_chartAlgFin_mem_ssJSet_over_of_ssPlaces), which adds supersingularity of $j$ at $y$, and it feeds the count of maximal ideals over a moduli place.
